  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Oxfordshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1896\n£40.00\n\nSorry, this item is out of stock\n\nCompiled and Edited by Captain A. F. Mockler-Ferryman\n\nPublished 1897 - Eyre and Spottiswoode, London\n\n \n\nContents:\n\nRegimental Calendar for 1897\nThe Army List January 1896\nThe Army List December 1896\nThe 1st Battalion in 1896\n\nRecord of the 1st Battalion in 1896\nThe 2nd Battalion in 1896\nRecord of 2nd Battalion in 1896\nThe Depot in 1896\nExtracts from the London Gazette in 1896\nChanges in Equipment in 1896\nMusketry 1896\nAthletics in 1896\nFootball in 1896\nCricket in 1896\nPolo in 1896\nSignalling in 1896\nThe 43rd Light Infantry Dinner 1896\nThe 52nd Light Infantry Dinner 1896\n\nMiscellaneous\nA Soldiers Journal\nCaptain William Thorne\nThe 52nd in 1805\nPeninsular Verses\nRegimental Officers on the Staff at Waterloo\nRegimental Uniform\nCaptain roger Frederic\nSir William Napier and Old Soldiers\nWar Medals\nRecollections of an Old Soldier\nA 52nd Subaltern 1851-2\nPunjab Movable Column under Nicholson\nMunity Letters\nReminiscences of New Zealand\nA Bicycle Ride to Mont St. Michel\nThree Days after Tiger in the Terai\nPigsticking at Bareilly\nA Shooting Trip; by Sergeants of the 2nd Battalion\nThe Battle of Ferket\nTo Dongola\nLight Infantry: its History and Early Drill\nGun and Rifle 2nd Battalion\nObituary\n\nNotice to Correspondents\n\nIllustrations\n\nMaps\n\n \n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nBugle & Sabre I\n£5.00 Add to cart\nThe Skipper’s War: Dragon School, Oxford & The Great War\n£20.00 Add to cart\nRedcoats to Riflemen: A Short History of the Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire County Regiment\n£4.50 Add to cart\nRemembered: The Men on the War Memorials of Witney, Crawley and Hailey. Volume 2: 1939-1945.\n£9.99 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
